course: dictionary
lesson: 14700
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Principal is one of them. It can be a person, a word meaning main, or a word about money. The context, meaning the words around it, tells you which meaning to use. «The principal visited our class today.» Here, a principal is a person: the head teacher of a school.
explain: «Our principal reason for going to the park was the sunshine.» Here principal is an adjective and means main or most important. The reason we went was mainly the sunshine. Try swapping in main: "Our main reason for going..." still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «Sam put £100 in the bank. The principal was £100, and the bank added interest on top.» In money, the principal is the amount you start with, before interest is added. Look for clues like money, bank or interest to spot this meaning.
fact: Principal can be a noun (a person, or a sum of money) or an adjective (meaning main).
fact: «The principal» can mean the head teacher of a school, especially in the USA, Canada, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: «The principal city» means the main city, and «the principal rivers» means the main rivers.
fact: In money, the principal is the amount you first borrow or save, before interest is added.
fact: Principal and principle sound the same but mean different things, so check the spelling and the context.
exercise: «The principal met the new children in the hall.» Who is the principal here? | A present from the teacher | * The head teacher of the school | A type of hall floor | The oldest child in the class
exercise: «Our principal reason for going to the park was the sunshine.» What does principal mean here? | * Main | Sunny | Last | Wet
exercise: Sam puts £100 in the bank. Which amount is the principal? | The interest the bank adds | * The £100 he first saved | The name of the bank | The number of years he waits
test: «The principal rivers of the country are wide and long.» What does principal mean here? | Smallest | Frozen | Hidden | * Main
test: «Our school principal read a story at assembly.» Who is the principal? | The name of the hall | A cup of tea | A type of school bus | * The head teacher
exam: «The principal city of the region is where most people work.» Which word means the same as principal here? | Smallest | * Main | Quietest | Oldest
